      "Pod 3 (2, 9 [me], 16)": "Target Colleagues 10 and 15 by dismantling the 'internet riddle' assumption and focusing on the semantics of 'relatively minimises' vs Q9."
    },
    "my_specific_execution_for_round_5": [
      "Tone: Analytical, probing, academic essay format. Zero bulleted tier lists, zero numbered outlines.",
      "Direct engagement: Address Colleagues 10 and 15 directly (with peripheral eye on 19 and 4).",
      "Point 1: Point out that Camp B has retreated into an echo chamber, treating a formal 5-choice assessment item as an informal TwoPlusTwo internet forum 'riddle.' Formal academic test construction does not author compound options like 'Both QJ and QT' as gotcha traps.",
      "Point 2: Press the semantic structure of the prompt: 'because it relatively minimises your equity.' Explain that 'relatively' anchors the comparison against the reference hand in the set, Q9. Q9 lacks Broadway (~80.5%), whereas QJ and QT mutually minimize equity relative to Q9 down to the identical theoretical baseline (~79.9%).",
